---
title: Maintenance Mode
description: Database-driven maintenance circuit breaker and API bypass mechanism.
section: Operations
order: 3
---

## Dynamic Maintenance Architecture

Lament features a database-driven maintenance switch. When maintenance mode is active for `lament_api`, all non-administrative requests are immediately intercepted by middleware returning HTTP 503 Service Unavailable.

---

## Toggling Maintenance Mode

### Check Status (`GET /maintenance`)

```http
GET /maintenance
```

```json
{
  "lament": false,
  "lament_api": true,
  "description": "Upgrading database schema for new lyric features",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-30T08:00:00Z"
}
```

### Enable / Disable Maintenance (`PUT /maintenance`)

Requires `X-Master-Key`:

```bash
curl -X PUT https://api.lament.rynds.my.id/maintenance \
  -H "X-Master-Key: <your_master_secret>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "lament_api": true,
    "description": "Scheduled maintenance for database migration"
  }'
```

---

## Bypassing Maintenance Mode

Developers can bypass maintenance mode locally or in production by setting the environment variable:

```env
BYPASS_MAINTENANCE=true
```
